---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <%= partial "partials/brand" %>
    <h1>
      Redact <span class="scribble" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="sensitive data (tap to reveal)">sensitive data<svg viewBox="0 0 600 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path pathLength="1" d="M4 10 C211 7 418 12 596 9 L596 24 C390 19 184 21 7 22 L8 41 C211 38 415 32 589 37 L598 56 C392 52 186 53 9 55 L7 72 C211 68 415 71 589 68 L589 84 C387 82 185 84 11 84 L4 96 C208 99 413 89 588 92"/></svg></span>.<br>
      Privately on your device.
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Free redaction tools powered by AI models that run locally in your browser.
      Your files never leave your computer. No uploads, no accounts, no servers reading your data.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="tools" class="tools">
  <div class="wrap">
    <ul class="grid">
      <% data.tools.each do |tool| %>
        <li class="card<%= " is-soon" unless tool.live %>">
          <div class="card-top">
            <span class="card-input"><%= tool.input %></span>
          </div>
          <h3>
            <% if tool.live %>
              <a href="/tools/<%= tool.slug %>/" class="card-link"><%= tool.name %></a>
            <% else %>
              <%= tool.name %>
            <% end %>
          </h3>
          <p><%= tool.description %></p>
          <div class="card-foot">
            <span class="card-model"><%= tool.model %></span>
            <% unless tool.live %><span class="soon">Coming soon</span><% end %>
          </div>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="how" class="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <ul class="points">
      <li>
        <h3>No data leaves your device</h3>
        <p>Your files and text are read by your browser and processed in your computer's memory. The tools have no server that receives them, and we keep no copy. To check, open your browser's network panel while you use a tool.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Works offline</h3>
        <p>Each AI model downloads once, and your browser keeps it. After the model loads, you can disconnect from the internet and keep working. This is a good way to redact very sensitive documents.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Small models, fast results</h3>
        <p>The tools use compact AI models that are made to run in a browser. The Text Redactor model is 29 MB. Detection runs with WebAssembly on an ordinary laptop or phone, with no special hardware.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>You make the final decision</h3>
        <p>Automatic detection can miss things or hide too much. Each tool shows its suggestions before you export. You can keep any item, add words to always hide, and read the result before you share it.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Open models</h3>
        <p>The tools use open-source models from Hugging Face. Each tool page tells you which model it uses, so you can check what the model was trained to find.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Free, with no account</h3>
        <p>There is no sign-up, no usage limit and no watermark. Your data never reaches us, so we have no reason to ask who you are.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="notify">
      <h2>Get Notified</h2>
      <p>Be first to know when we launch new free tools for redaction.</p>
      <a href="https://mailchi.mp/52e24e1cbb61/redacted-mailing-list" class="button button-big" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sign Up for the Newsletter</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  // Tap, click or press Enter to reveal the words under the scribble.
  document.querySelectorAll(".scribble").forEach((el) => {
    const toggle = () => el.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(el.getAttribute("aria-pressed") !== "true"));
    el.addEventListener("click", toggle);
    el.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
      if (e.key === "Enter" || e.key === " ") {
        e.preventDefault();
        toggle();
      }
    });
  });
</script>
